WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.303
-So great to see you.
I am so excited for this.

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.071
"The Kids Tonight Show" --
it's happening.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.139
-Yes!

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.173
-You guys --
Alright, let's just go.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.075
Olivia, maybe you start it off.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.543
Tell everyone what
"The Kids Tonight Show"

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.845
is about.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.080
-So, it's a talk show,
like "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.648
but more kid-ified.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.084
So, it's four hosts --
four kid hosts.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:21.587
We've got Dylan, Mykal-Michelle,
Me, and Recker.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.822
-That's right.
-And it's, like, really messy.

00:00:23.822 --> 00:00:25.157
There's a bunch of games.

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:26.626
And I think you all
would love it.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:27.694
It's so much fun.

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:30.196
-Yeah. Come on.
How cute are these kids?

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.465
Are you joking me?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.233
Every single one.
-Thank you.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.601
-Alright, Dylan.
-Yeah?

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.837
-What was your reaction
when you got the job,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.105
when you first found out that

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.773
you're going be the host of
"The Kids Tonight Show"?

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:44.544
-So, I was doing another job
while I heard this.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.246
And I was like -- So, I was in
the dressing room like,

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:49.081
"Oh, my gosh.
I can't believe it.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:50.116
Like, really?

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.717
Produced by
Jimmy Fallon himself?

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.119
Like, really?"

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:56.856
And my grandmother be going to
sleep, like, at like 9:00,

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.758
and she stays up
just to watch your show.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.194
She stays up to 11:00 p.m.
just to watch your show, man.

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:02.328
-She does?
-Yes.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.929
-Tell her, "Thank you."
See, I love that.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.231
-Shout-out to Grandma.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:06.799
-Shout-out to Grand--
Shout-out to Grandma.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.301
Mykal-Michelle, how --
Be honest.

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:11.137
What's it like working with me?

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.504
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:14.440
-I mean, you are okay.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.909
-Oh, stop, stop, stop.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.677
-No, I'm just kidding.
I'm just kidding.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:20.213
I'm just kidding.
You were awesome.

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:23.048
I mean, Mr. Jimmy,
take no offense to this,

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:25.385
but you're like a big kid.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.620
You're awesome. You get us.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.089
-No, I love to see --
We all loved you,

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:32.858
because you were -- We shot
the show across the hall,

00:01:32.858 --> 00:01:36.428
and it just made everyone
so happy to just see you guys.

00:01:36.428 --> 00:01:38.664
You're so talented,
every single one of you.

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:41.900
Recker -- Dude, Recker,
you play the drums on this show,

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:44.537
so you're kind of a band leader,
as well as a host.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.439
Did you get any advice
from Questlove?

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.473
-I did.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:49.475
Well, first of all,
he's so tall.

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:52.178
Like, he's so tall.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.446
But --
-Are you?

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.647
Yeah, he is fairly tall. Yeah.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.282
-Yeah, I'm kind of tall.
-Yeah, you are tall.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.650
Yeah. Interesting. Yeah.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.951
That's what you
took away from Questlove?

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.286
That he's tall?
-No, not that.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.688
But, I mean, yeah,
he's tall, but he, like --

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:03.956
He told me how he got started

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:05.324
busking on the street
with Tariq.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:07.694
But that's kind of the same way
I started, too, like,

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.328
busking on the street
with my band.

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:12.498
And then now, like, we're here.
It's crazy.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.267
[ Applause ]
-Whoo!

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:18.604
-When you guys interviewed the
guests, were you nervous at all?

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.973
I mean, because you talked to,
I mean, JoJo Siwa.

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:24.377
You talked to --
You talked to an astronaut.

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.878
-Yeah!
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:27.813
-That was so awesome.

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:29.249
-Yeah. That's cool, right?

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:33.753
-You know, like, once, we got to
interview a kid who had, like,

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.588
over like 200 million followers.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.890
We were like, "What?!"
So, I mean --

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.593
-That was a note that has
never been hit ever

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.195
on "The Tonight Show,"
by the way.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:45.632
I can't say
more compliments about you

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.100
and how professional
and how awesome

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.101
you guys were to work with.

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:49.169
-Thank you.
-Thank you so much.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:50.970
-I loved you so much,
top to bottom.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.039
Everyone loves you. Thank you.
Congratulations.

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:55.407
-Thank you.
-It's happening, guys.

00:02:55.407 --> 00:02:58.244
-Yeah!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.745
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:02.215
Here's a peek at
"The Kids Tonight Show."

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.249
Take a look.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:06.552 line:0%
-My first dog was named Jeff,

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:10.122 line:0%
and he loved wearing sunglasses
and a baseball hat.

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:12.392 line:0%
-Okay. Alright.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.826 line:0%
-Jim-Jim?
-I know who that is.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.727
-Jim-Jim?

00:03:15.727 --> 00:03:17.397
Don't call me Jim-Jim.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:19.365
[ All shouting ]

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.171
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.171 --> 00:03:29.808
-Yes! Yes!

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:31.711
-Okay, okay. Alright.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.613
Alright.
-Yes!

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:36.315
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:39.718
-Check out Dylan,
Mykal-Michelle, Olivia, Recker.

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:41.421
"The Kids Tonight Show,"

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:44.757
starting October 14th,
next Thursday, on Peacock.

